#. Add-on description
#. Translators: Long description to be shown for this add-on on add-on information from add-ons manager
#: buildVars.py:26
msgid ""
"This add-on makes it possible to describe the focused control, navigator "
"object, or entire screen using popular AI vision models including OpenAI "
"GPT, Google Gemini, Anthropic Claude, xAI Grok, Mistral Pixtral, local "
"options like Ollama/llama.cpp/LiteLLM, and more. It also supports follow-up "
"questions on any description, camera snapshots, clipboard images, and face "
"positioning via a connected camera.\n"
"Content descriptions may not always be completely accurate or reflect real-"
"world information.\n"
"Press NVDA+shift+i to pop up a menu for choosing what to describe, "
"NVDA+shift+u to describe the navigator object, NVDA+shift+y for an image on "
"the clipboard, or NVDA+alt+c to ask follow-up questions about the last "
"description. Other keystrokes are available from the input gestures dialog.\n"
"By default, usage is free through PollinationsAI with no sign-up or API key "
"required. To use other models, visit the provider's website to obtain an API "
"key, then enter it under the AI Content Describer category in NVDA's "
"settings dialog. See the add-on documentation for more information."
msgstr ""
